# A walk through the whole approval chain, using the sample people.
#
# 1. In a terminal:  dotnet run --project src/PBRMS.Api
# 2. Needs the REST Client extension in VS Code. Click "Send Request" above each
#    block, IN ORDER FROM THE TOP: later steps use the answers from earlier ones.
#    The answer opens on the right.
#
# To go through it again, change @day to a date you haven't used. Or leave it the
# same to see a clash at step 7: the answer names the production in the way.

@api = http://localhost:5188
@day = 2026-12-01


### Is the API up, and can it reach the database?
GET {{api}}/health


### ---- Sign everyone in (Development only: no password) ----

### Producer
# @name producer
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "producer@pbrms.test" }

### Production Manager
# @name pm
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "pm@pbrms.test" }

### Executive Producer
# @name ep
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ep@pbrms.test" }

### Camera supervisor
# @name supervisor
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@pbrms.test" }

### Booking Officer
# @name bookingOfficer
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "booking@pbrms.test" }


### Who am I? Shows the supervisor's roles.
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}


### Departments and divisions, sorted by name: Camera, News, Sound, Sports.
# @name units
GET {{api}}/org-units
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}


### ---- The approval chain ----

### 1. The producer fills in the booking form. Status: Draft.
# @name booking
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Morning Show",
  "departmentId": "{{units.response.body.$[1].id}}",
  "activityType": "Recording",
  "venue": "Studio1",
  "callAt": "{{day}}T06:00:00+02:00",
  "startsAt": "{{day}}T06:30:00+02:00",
  "endsAt": "{{day}}T09:00:00+02:00",
  "crewSlots": [
    { "divisionId": "{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}", "positionLabel": "Camera 1" }
  ]
}

### 2. The producer submits it. Status: PmReview.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Submit" }

### 3. It's in the Production Manager's queue.
GET {{api}}/bookings/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{pm.response.body.token}}

### 4. The Production Manager approves. Status: EpReview.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{pm.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve", "note": "Looks fine" }

### 5. The Executive Producer approves and sets the channel. Status: CrewAssignment.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{ep.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve", "channel": "Nbc1" }

### 6. The supervisor opens the crew picker: Camera's operators.
# @name operators
GET {{api}}/org-units/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/operators
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### 7. The supervisor assigns the first operator. That fills the last position. Status: Finalisation.
PUT {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/crew
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assignments": [
    { "slotId": "{{booking.response.body.$.crewSlots[0].id}}", "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}" }
  ]
}

### 8. The Booking Officer checks for clashes. [] means none.
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/clashes
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}

### 9. The Booking Officer confirms. Status: Confirmed.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve" }

### 10. The finished booking: crew, and every step in "history".
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}


### ---- Things that must be refused ----

### Approving a booking that is already confirmed. Answer: 409, with the reason.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve" }

### A form that ends before it starts. Answer: 400, with the reason.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Backwards",
  "departmentId": "{{units.response.body.$[1].id}}",
  "activityType": "Recording",
  "venue": "Studio2",
  "callAt": "{{day}}T08:00:00+02:00",
  "startsAt": "{{day}}T10:00:00+02:00",
  "endsAt": "{{day}}T09:00:00+02:00"
}

### No token. Answer: 401.
GET {{api}}/me


### ---- Monthly roster (needs the sign-ins and "units" above, and step 6) ----
# Use a month with no bookings yet. Change @month to start a fresh roster.

@month = 2027-04

### The Camera legend: what each shift code means.
GET {{api}}/shift-definitions/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R1. The supervisor fills in two cells. Status: Draft.
PUT {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entries": [
    { "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}", "date": "{{month}}-01", "code": "L" },
    { "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}", "date": "{{month}}-02", "code": "A1" }
  ]
}

### R2. See the grid.
GET {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R3. Publish it. Status: Published. "clashes" lists any confirmed booking it upsets.
POST {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R4. Is that operator free on the 1st? No: they're on leave.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-01T09:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-01T11:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R5. On the 2nd, inside their 08h00–17h00 shift? Yes: [] means free.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-02T09:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-02T11:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R6. In the evening of the 2nd? No: outside their shift.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-02T19:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-02T21:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}
